sip: send a request whose next hop is a sips: URI over TLS

libre refuses any request whose next hop is not a sip: URI
(sip_request_alloc returns ENOSYS). Flexisip (sip.linphone.org)
Record-Routes with <sips:host:5061;lr> and OpenAI's SIP endpoint answers
with a sips: Contact, so on those paths nothing sent inside a dialog
goes out: no ACK when calling, no BYE, no re-INVITE.

A sips: next hop is accepted and reached over TLS (RFC 3261 19.1.2 and
26.2.2). TLS is forced whatever transport the dialog is already on and
whatever a transport parameter says, because a caller that reached the
proxy over UDP, or a URI that picked up transport=udp from an account,
would otherwise send to the TLS port in the clear. Without a TLS
transport the request fails with EPROTONOSUPPORT.

Origin: based on https://github.com/baresip/re/pull/1647 by phgace
("sip: send requests with a sips: route over TLS"), which upstream
closed without merging ("We decided in the past not to add sips
support"; see also https://github.com/baresip/re/issues/1659). That
change took the dialog's transport as given and mapped only
transport=tcp to TLS; this one forces TLS in every case.

libre is BSD-3-Clause; this patch is offered under the same terms.

--- a/src/sip/request.c
+++ b/src/sip/request.c
@@ -646,12 +646,15 @@
 {
 	struct sip_request *req;
 	struct pl pl;
+	bool sips;
 	int err;
 
 	if (!sip || !met || !uri || !route || !mb)
 		return EINVAL;
 
-	if (pl_strcasecmp(&route->scheme, "sip"))
+	sips = !pl_strcasecmp(&route->scheme, "sips");
+
+	if (!sips && pl_strcasecmp(&route->scheme, "sip"))
 		return ENOSYS;
 
 	req = mem_zalloc(sizeof(*req), destructor);
@@ -710,6 +713,20 @@
 		req->tp_selected = false;
 	}
 
+	/* A SIPS URI is reached over TLS (RFC 3261 19.1.2 and 26.2.2),
+	 * whatever transport the dialog is on or a transport parameter
+	 * names */
+	if (sips && req->tp != SIP_TRANSP_TLS && req->tp != SIP_TRANSP_WSS) {
+
+		if (!sip_transp_supported(sip, SIP_TRANSP_TLS, AF_UNSPEC)) {
+			err = EPROTONOSUPPORT;
+			goto out;
+		}
+
+		req->tp = SIP_TRANSP_TLS;
+		req->tp_selected = true;
+	}
+
 out:
 	if (err)
 		mem_deref(req);
